@startuml feasibility_check
title FeasibilityCheck.check - confirmation verdict (FEASIBLE / INFEASIBLE / UNPROVEN)

start
:Read graph; build RawRuleTable + coarse/fine models
(same code and constants as production);
if (generator rejects graph?\n(bad range, unmeetable requirement,\nminimum cells > grid)) then (yes)
  :INFEASIBLE
  proof = generator's own message;
  stop
endif

partition "proof engine (counting model, Choco) [3]" {
  :laws = every size range, required border,
  illegal pair of the graph;
  :CountingModel.check(all laws);
  note right
    Sound by construction: every counting rule is
    implied by the coarse solver's own rules
    (per-cluster size and perimeter, required borders,
    legal pairs, hex corners = 3 mutually legal biomes).
    UNKNOWN (solver timeout) is never treated as a proof.
  end note
  if (CONTRADICTION?) then (yes)
    :per-biome pass: each biome's own laws on a model
    focused on that biome (ms per check),
    if contradicting: QuickXplain inside them,
    verify on the full model, set those laws aside;
    repeat
      :QuickXplain on the remaining laws (full model);
      :record it as one conflict;
      :drop those laws from the rest;
    repeat while (rest still CONTRADICTION\nAND time left?) is (yes)
    :INFEASIBLE
    proof = every independent minimal conflict
    (marked incomplete if time ran out);
    stop
  endif
}

partition "world search (production-identical attempts)" {
  :Run coarse / refinement / render attempts
  on every thread until the deadline;
  if (a full world was built\n(coarse + refinement + render)?) then (yes)
    :FEASIBLE
    show the built world (picture),
    secondary: "N of M attempts", production
    world-seed failure range (only here);
    stop
  else (deadline)
    :UNPROVEN
    plain facts: "0 of 48 coarse attempts solved,
    no contradiction found", no probability headline;
    stop
  endif
}
@enduml
